
Description:

New jmap_require_accountid option.  When enabled, JMAP method calls
without an accountId are rejected with invalidArguments, instead of
running against the authenticated user's own account.

Core/echo is the sole exception, and continues to not require an accountId.

Documentation:

lib/imapoptions/jmap_require_accountid.  The behaviour follows RFC 8620
Section 3.6.2 as written.


Config changes:

jmap_require_accountid (switch, default off): reject JMAP method calls
that omit accountId rather than defaulting to the authenticated user's
account.


Upgrade instructions:

At some future time, jmap_require_accountid will be the default.

Explicitly set jmap_require_accountid to 'no' if your clients
are not sending accountId on every method call, or fix the clients.

